cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "Le Chapeau: An Open-Source A/B Testing Platform for Conversational AI and LLM Interactions"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-13"
url: "https://github.com/mickaeltemporao/paper-socrates"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mickaeltemporao/paper-socrates"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
authors:
  - family-names: "Temporão"
    given-names: "Mickael"
abstract: >-
  Le Chapeau is a turnkey, open-source A/B testing platform engineered for
  conducting controlled experiments and randomized trials with conversational
  AI agents and Large Language Models (LLMs). The platform enables researchers
  to systematically assign participants to distinct conversational conditions
  (such as differing prompt strategies, persona scaffolding, or model variants)
  through pre-registered rosters or balanced dynamic allocation. It features
  real-time atomic interaction logging with zero data loss, GDPR/IRB-compliant
  salted deterministic pseudonymization (UUIDv5) for longitudinal participant
  tracking, and turnkey deployment via native scripts, Docker Compose, or
  multi-worker clusters.
keywords:
  - "a/b testing"
  - "randomized controlled trials"
  - "conversational ai"
  - "human-ai interaction"
  - "large language models"
  - "experimental platform"
  - "interaction design"
  - "prompt engineering"
  - "behavioral research"
  - "educational technology"
